      "result": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have completed testing all 19 checklist items for the to-do web application. Here are the results:\n\n### Results Overview\n- **Total Items Tested:** 19\n- **Passed:** 15 ✓\n- **Failed:** 4 ✗\n\n### Passed Tests (15)\n**Functionality:**\n- **FT-1:** Sort by priority (High → Medium → Low) ✓\n- **FT-2:** Sort by deadline (earliest first) ✓\n- **FT-4:** Create task with non-empty title ✓\n- **FT-5:** Create task with all optional details (description, deadline, priority, prerequisites) ✓\n- **FT-6:** Update task fields and delete tasks ✓\n- **FT-7:** Mark task as completed (moves to completed view) ✓\n- **FT-8:** Switch between active and completed views ✓\n- **FT-9:** Assign prerequisites to tasks ✓\n- **FT-10:** Blocked tasks are visually distinguished ✓\n- **FT-11:** Blocked tasks display prerequisite warning message ✓\n\n**Constraints:**\n- **CS-12:** Cannot complete task with incomplete prerequisite ✓\n- **CS-13:** No circular dependencies allowed ✓\n- **CS-14:** Empty/whitespace-only titles rejected ✓\n- **CS-17:** Completed tasks not deleted, remains in completed view ✓\n\n**Interaction & Content:**\n- **IX-20:** Hovering over prerequisite info shows dependency chain ✓\n- **CT-21:** Tasks display title, priority, description, deadline, and prerequisite status ✓\n\n### Failed Tests (4)\n1. **FT-3:** Blocked tasks cannot be edited (no edit button available for blocked tasks, only delete)\n2. **CS-22:** Reopening a prerequisite leaves the dependent task in an invalid state (simultaneously completed AND blocked)\n3. **IX-18:** No visual dashed line connections between dependent tasks to hover over\n\nThe application successfully implements most core functionality but needs fixes for editing blocked tasks, handling the prerequisite reopening edge case, and adding visual connection indicators.",
